#: GameServer.RpcHandlers
msgid "level completed with warnings… 🎭"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DFA.L01_Run
msgid "Running a machine"
msgstr ""

#: Game
msgid "Games of Computation"
msgstr ""

#: GameServer.RpcHandlers
msgid "level completed! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#: GameServer.RpcHandlers
msgid "intermediate goal solved! 🎉"
msgstr ""

#: Game
msgid "Finite automata, proved"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `even`
#. §1: `ab`
#. §2: `odd`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L01_Run
msgid "Starting in §0, after reading §1 the machine is in §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rfl`
#. §1: `A = A`
#. §2: `rfl`
#: Game.Doc.Tactics
msgid "§0 closes a goal of the form §1, where both sides are equal\n"
"*by definition*. Lean is allowed to unfold definitions and compute while\n"
"checking this, so §2 can prove that a machine ends in a particular state\n"
"after reading a short, concrete string."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `parityA`
#. §1: `even`
#. §2: `odd`
#. §3: `a`
#. §4: `b`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L01_Run
msgid "A deterministic finite automaton reads a string one symbol at a time,\n"
"moving from state to state.\n"
"\n"
"Our first machine, §0, has two states: §1 and §2.\n"
"Reading §3 swaps them; reading §4 changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: Game
msgid "Prove the classic results about finite automata and regular languages,\n"
"one level at a time."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `parityA`
#. §1: `even`
#. §2: `odd`
#. §3: `a`
#. §4: `b`
#. §5: `even`
#. §6: `even`
#: Game.Doc.Definitions
msgid "§0 has two states, §1 and §2. Reading §3 swaps them,\n"
"reading §4 leaves the state alone. It starts in §5 and accepts in §6."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DFA
msgid "Deterministic Automata"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a`
#. §1: `even`
#. §2: `odd`
#. §3: `b`
#. §4: `rfl`
#: Game.Levels.DFA.L01_Run
msgid "Both sides compute to the same state: §0 takes §1 to §2,\n"
"then §3 leaves it there. When two sides are equal just by computing,\n"
"§4 proves it."
msgstr ""

#: Game
msgid "A game on finite automata and regular languages, built with lean4game."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DFA
msgid "In this world you will run machines, then prove what they do on every input."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DFA.L01_Run
msgid "Lean ran the machine for you. Soon you'll prove things about runs of\n"
"*every* length, where computing is no longer enough."
msgstr ""

#: Game
msgid "Learn DFAs, NFAs, closure properties and non-regularity by proving them in Lean."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `M.evalFrom q w`
#. §1: `M`
#. §2: `w`
#. §3: `q`
#. §4: `M.evalFrom q [] = q`
#. §5: `M.evalFrom q (x :: xs) = M.evalFrom (M.step q x) xs`
#: Game.Doc.Definitions
msgid "§0 is the state the machine §1 is in after reading the\n"
"string §2, starting from state §3. It reads one symbol at a time:\n"
"\n"
"* §4\n"
"* §5"
msgstr ""
